From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mbt28 <btekbas@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 4 Jul 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] lctech_pi_f1c200s: enable the 800x480 LCD

Enable the sunxi DE1 video console on the board's 5.0" 800x480 panel
(EastRising ER-TFT050-6). Timings match the Linux panel-simple entry the
board's DT uses: 25 MHz pixel clock, H 8/4/8 (front/sync/back),
V 16/4/8, both syncs active low (sync:0), 16-bit RGB565 bus (the
40-pin FPC wires only the 16 MSB lines).

The backlight on PE6 is a plain enable GPIO (active high) - the same
way the kernel drives it via gpio-backlight - so it is configured as
VIDEO_LCD_BL_EN rather than a PWM output.

VIDEO_DT_SIMPLEFB (implied by VIDEO_SUNXI) is explicitly disabled:
injecting a simple-framebuffer node + top-of-DRAM reservation into the
kernel DT breaks the boot on this 64 MiB board (the kernel has its own
DRM driver and an extremely tight early memory layout - hangs at
"Starting kernel"). The U-Boot splash still shows until Linux's DRM
takes over.

Signed-off-by: mbt28 <btekbas@gmail.com>
---
 configs/lctech_pi_f1c200s_defconfig | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/configs/lctech_pi_f1c200s_defconfig
+++ b/configs/lctech_pi_f1c200s_defconfig
@@ -6,7 +6,10 @@
 CONFIG_MACH_SUNIV=y
 CONFIG_DRAM_ZQ=0
 CONFIG_SUNXI_MINIMUM_DRAM_MB=64
-# CONFIG_VIDEO_SUNXI is not set
+CONFIG_VIDEO_SUNXI=y
+CONFIG_VIDEO_LCD_MODE="x:800,y:480,depth:16,pclk_khz:25000,le:8,ri:8,up:8,lo:16,hs:4,vs:4,sync:0,vmode:0"
+CONFIG_VIDEO_LCD_BL_EN="PE6"
+# CONFIG_VIDEO_DT_SIMPLEFB is not set
 CONFIG_MTD=y
 CONFIG_CONS_INDEX=2
 CONFIG_SPI=y
-- 
